.TH COSMOS-CAMERA 1 "November 2026" "Cosmos Camera" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cosmos-camera \- Jetson desktop camera and Cosmos visual reasoning assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cosmos-camera
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows a USB camera preview and runs sampled images through a local Cosmos model.
On first use, a setup dialog downloads and verifies the pinned model and container.
Model access must be granted by the original model publisher.
Requires Jetson Orin, Ubuntu 22.04 and L4T R36.4.x.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --setup
Open the first-run setup dialog again.
.TP
.B --check
Print environment diagnostics without opening a window or loading the model.
.TP
.B --no-camera
Open the application without automatically starting the camera.
.TP
.BI --source " DEVICE"
Override the saved camera source for this session.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cosmos-camera/settings.json
User settings, including model path, camera and prompt.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cosmos-camera/models/
Downloaded model versions.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/cosmos-camera/logs/
Analysis and model service logs.
.SH NOTES
Run the application as a regular desktop user. Standard XDG directory overrides
are supported. Removing the package preserves user models, settings and logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cosmos-camera-setup-host (1)
